# AVP Parsing Safety Patterns

## Bounds Checking Requirements
Always perform bounds checking when parsing AVP data to prevent "list index out of range" errors.

### Pattern: Safe Array Access
```python
def safe_parse_function(raw_bytes):
    # ALWAYS check bounds first
    if not raw_bytes or len(raw_bytes) < minimum_required_length:
        logger.warning(f"Invalid data - too short: {len(raw_bytes) if raw_bytes else 0} bytes")
        return None
    
    # Now safe to access
    first_byte = raw_bytes[0]
    second_byte = raw_bytes[1]
```

